When the directory entries have been completed, press ESCAPE twice to return to
the dialling prompt. Press "L" to load a number to the modem. If the modem is  
off the user will be prompted to turn it on and press RETURN.                  
                                                                         nd after the BELL tone enter (1-8) to dial the selected number.       
If the modem does not respond a timeout message will be displayed. If this     
happens, check the cable connections and power connection to the modem.        
The modem will dial th      
The dialling entry is then selected (1-8) followed by "," and then the modem   
directory number. (ie. entering "3,7" will load dialling entry 3 to the modem  
in position 7). This operation takes a few seconds depending on the number of  
charae selected number, and when a connection has been made   
will send any "id" characters. The incoming pages will be displayed on the     
left half of the screen. To switch screens, enter CTRL-P at the end of each    
page. A prompt "P>" will appear at cters to be loaded. If the dialling prompt or a timeout message is not    
displayed after a wait of 20 seconds, press ESCAPE twice and repeat the load   
operation.                                                                     
In order to make tthe bottom of the page to be overwritten.   
                                                                               
Entering the HASH character seizes the line for manual dialling or when the    
modem is connected to a leased line which is dirhe most efficient use of the dialling directory it is better 
to leave at least one modem directory slot free for infrequently used numbers. 
NOTE that your passwords and ID's are hidden by "*" characters when they are   
displayed. They are visible wheectly connected at both ends.  
Pressing ESCAPE twice will return to the MAIN MENU at most points in the dial  
sequence. Remember to disconnect (MAIN MENU function 17) when finished, as     
charges will be incurred for telephone access.               n a new entry is made to the directory until    
overlayed by a new directory page, and will always be hidden by stars for each 
subsequent display.                                                            
